 rope and JSON chunk","+  iteration share one lazy edit overlay so the two views cannot diverge. RCH scans serialized bytes","+  with bounded buffering and retains edits in another `MappingSource`, including custom digests","+  and maps participating in content-hash groups. Reuse the scan's byte count when creating edited","+  views so their size calculation does not serialize the input again. Edited writers apply byte","+  ranges to the original SIMD serializer's output; do not route them through the scalar rope escaper.","+  SRI computes all requested digests in one serialization pass. Content equality retains field references and","+  advances through escapes lazily, rather than retaining a reference per escaped fragment.","+  Content hashing and equality consume the exact rendered bytes; structural Source hashing remains","+  separate. Persistent cache stores map fields and edit layers directly, preserving empty fields","+  without JSON encoding or parsing. Its map record is boxed so other cached source nodes do not","+  grow. For external `noSources` maps, own the remaining borrowed metadata before releasing the","+  owner of the removed contents. Do not retain the whole JSON in either the map asset or its","+  replacement result. JS binding content requests remain an explicit materialization boundary."," - `ConcatSource::add` uses `&mut self` and `Mutex::get_mut`; reads lazily optimize children. Mapping","   shifts generated positions and remaps child-local indices into global deduplicated tables."," - `ReplaceSource` ranges are half-open byte ranges. Edits are ordered by"],"additions":20,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -5810,6 +5810,7 @@ dependencies = ["," name = \"rspack_util\""," version = \"0.102.9\""," dependencies = [","+ \"aho-corasick\",","  \"anyhow\",","  \"base64-simd 0.8.0\",","  \"bitflags 2.13.2\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/rspack_core/src/utils/source.rs","lines":["@@ -1,